Z||000000||fierospeeder||12-27-2001||06:35 PM||||Im not sure if anyone have heard anything about this besides people from illinois.<P>A young woman and her child were traveling on a bus from st louis to chicago.  While in chicago, waiting in the bus terminal.  I guess for another bus to wisconsin.  She met another woman which she talked to for a half an hour.  <P>The woman with the child (i cant recall why she did this) gave it to the woman, because she was busy with something or had to go to the bathroom.<P>Few minutes later, she realized the woman with her child just ran out of the bus terminal.  This was a day before Xmas.<P>There was a great picture of the kidnapper, and a tatto on the woman's neck (christin).<BR>After a few days, i was pissed cause there was no leads, and a tatto on the neck is very obvious.<P><BR>About an hour ago, on the news.  The kidnapper and her boyfriend have been arrested by police/FBI in West Virginia.  And the child has been found,  Safe.  <BR>(the news guy paused, like the child was dead but said safe and sound. freaked me out)<P>i probably can post a link if anyone wants one for local news in illinois.||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||12-27-2001||06:44 PM||||Ive seen it on the news, but didnt know they found it. Glad for her. Ill bet shes lots more careful in the future. She got her Happy New Year a little early.||||reg||1
Z||000002||frontal lobe||12-28-2001||02:04 AM||||Reportedly the woman that kidnapped the baby was "going" with a man who got sent to jail.  When he was in jail, she told him that she was pregnant and was having a baby.  When he got out of jail, he wanted to see the child.  So the woman said she was with her mother in Chicago, and when they went there, he could see the baby.  So she needed to kidnap a baby to back up her story.  People are just unbelievable.<P>I am SO glad the woman got her baby back.  What a nightmare, even if it was her fault.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierobaby||12-28-2001||10:52 AM||||ok the woman with the baby IS A DUMB@$$! you never ever ever leave your child with someone else! AHHHHHHH I just want to scream in her face and beat her! GAWD! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||12-28-2001||11:53 AM||||I'll say she was stupid.  She had too much to carry so when this woman offered to help she handed over her CHILD, instead of some luggage.  She says the kidnapper was "warm and friendly".  I don't think her mother ever told her not to trust strangers!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  Did anyone see the biological father on TV the other day with the mother?  He had to ask on air what day his child was kidnapped!  He didn't seem to really be upset his child had been kidnapped!  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||TRiAD||12-29-2001||11:04 AM||||Here's more...<P><I>"Stolen child found unhurt <BR>Police: Kidnapper tried to prove pregnancy tale for jailed boyfriend <P>December 28, 2001<P>By NOAH ISACKSON <BR>of the Associated Press<P><BR>CHICAGO - A nationwide search for a toddler kidnapped on Christmas Eve ended on Thursday when the child was found unharmed in West Virginia. <P>Sixteen-month-old Jasmine Anderson was found at a home in the town of Williamson, said Thomas J. Kneir, special agent in charge of the FBI's Chicago office. <P>The girl was placed in the custody of the West Virginia Department of Health and Human Resources until she could be reunited with her parents. <P>Police arrested Sheila Annalee Matthews, 33, who has been charged with one count of federal kidnapping. She was taken into custody Thursday afternoon on a warrant issued in Chicago and was being held in the South Central Regional Jail in Charleston, W.Va. <P>A woman with the same name pleaded guilty in 1988 to a kidnapping charge in Washington, D.C. That woman abducted a 2½-year-old girl from her parents in Seattle in 1987. The Chicago Police Department could not confirm whether that woman and the one arrested Thursday are the same. FBI officials were unavailable by telephone late Thursday. <P>A tip from a relative of Matthews' boyfriend led to the arrest. <P>"We're really grateful to everyone who helped," said the child's mother, Marcella Anderson, fighting back tears. "Especially the family members who were brave enough to come forward and had really good hearts, and God bless everyone." <P>According to police, Matthews had told her boyfriend she had a baby while he was in a California prison, and when the man was released, she told him her mother was caring for the baby in Chicago. <P>"When she went to the Greyhound station that night, she was looking to abduct a baby," said Philip Cline, chief of detectives for the Chicago Police Department. "And unfortunately Marcella was there with Jasmine." <P>Anderson said she and her two daughters were waiting for a bus to Milwaukee on Monday when a woman approached the family. The woman offered to give them a ride home to Milwaukee. <P>The woman also suggested that she hold Jasmine while Anderson take her other daughter with her to the ticket counter. Anderson was waiting in line to return the tickets when the woman disappeared with the toddler, Anderson said. <P>At a news conference at Chicago police headquarters, Anderson said she was relieved and grateful Jasmine was found. She looked forward to going home to Milwaukee and celebrating Christmas. <P>Asked what she learned from the ordeal, Anderson replied, "No matter what, you have to try to deal with everything on your own." <P>The abduction set off a massive search that involved some 100 Chicago police officers. The case received national attention, and the department received tips from as far away as the West Coast. <P>On Thursday, Cline said that attention "helped crack this case." <P>According to police, Matthews and her boyfriend took the toddler to the house of one of his relatives in the Chicago suburb of Broadview on Christmas Day. <P>Matthews "tried to pretend that the baby was her own," Cline said, dressing the girl in a Christmas dress and even posing with her in a photo later obtained by police. <P>Early Wednesday morning, the couple traveled with Jasmine to West Virginia. Their hosts, meanwhile, spotted a photograph of Jasmine on television and called police on Thursday. <P>Chicago police officers found Jasmine's jacket at the Broadview home, Cline said. <P>Matthews is scheduled to appear in U.S. Magistrate Court in Charleston on Friday, according to senior supervisory agent Joe Ciccarelli of the FBI's Charleston, W.Va., office. <P>Her boyfriend was questioned and released, said Randy Coleman, a spokesman for the West Virginia Department of Military Affairs and Public Safety. <P>Hundreds of thousands of children are reported missing each year, but only 200 to 300 of those cases turn out to be abductions by strangers. There have been five confirmed cases in Chicago involving strangers over the past 15 years."</I><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://centralillinoisimports.org/uploads/files/SigRear4.gif">   <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B><BR>AIM ~ Michael Blue 72</I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 12-29-2001).]||||reg||1
